{{!< default}}

{{!-- The Post Surface, in whichever layout the publication picked.

The layout picker is the pattern home.hbs documents: one {{#match}} at the top, the
non-default option matched explicitly so an unrecognised stored value falls through to a
layout rather than to nothing, and no partial below reading @custom.

What is on this page below the article — the writer, the neighbours, three more posts, the
subscribe band — is the same in both layouts and belongs to neither, so it is called here
once. Only the reading column differs, which is the whole of what A1 and A2 are.

`.mirror-content` (in both layout partials) is the scoping hook the Koenig card layer needs:
Ghost emits cards.min.css out of {{ghost_head}}, BELOW this theme's stylesheet, so every rule
that has to beat a platform default is written under that class. assets/css/screen.css owns
that layer. --}}

{{> "chrome/header" compact=true}}

<main id="main" class="grow">
	{{#post}}
		<article class="{{post_class}}" data-surface="post">
			{{#match @custom.post_layout "Title page"}}
				{{> "post/a2"}}
			{{else}}
				{{> "post/a1"}}
			{{/match}}
		</article>

		{{> "post/related"}}

		{{> "newsletter" anchor="end-newsletter"}}
	{{/post}}
</main>

{{> "chrome/footer"}}
